&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Klaviyo, we value the unique backgrounds, experiences and perspectives each Klaviyo (we call ourselves Klaviyos) brings to our workplace each and every day. We believe everyone deserves a fair shot at success and appreciate the experiences each person brings beyond the traditional job requirements. If you’re a close but not exact match with the description, we hope you’ll still consider applying. Want to learn more about life at Klaviyo? Visit &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://klaviyo.com/careers&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;klaviyo.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to see how we empower creators to own their own destiny.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staff Engineer, Applied AI (Customer Agent)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Engineering team builds the AI systems that power how brands run their businesses on Klaviyo. We move fast, ship in production, and hold a high bar for what &quot;AI-native&quot; actually means: systems that make real judgment calls, not demos.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Customer Agent team is one of the newest and most ambitious groups in that org, based in Boston and working in-office: we&#39;re building a conversational AI system that lets brands serve their own customers at a scale no human support team could match. We&#39;re still small enough that one engineer’s work visibly shapes how the whole platform evolves. We&#39;re past the demo stage: the team ships changes against live customer traffic, measures quality with real evaluation frameworks, and treats reliability as a product feature, not an afterthought.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Engineer, you&#39;ll set the technical and product direction for a core area of Customer Agent end to end, building a 0-to-1 agentic product with the speed and ownership of a startup, backed by the scale and resources of one of the most innovative tech companies on the East Coast, while staying hands-on with the hardest problems yourself. This is a lead-level role, with a wide footprint across our agentic product - from orchestration to governance - that grows based on where the product is when you join. We&#39;re looking for an engineer who owns complex, ambiguous problems, who has built, scaled, and supported a production agentic system through everything that comes after the demo, and who up-levels the people, process, and technology around them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You&#39;ll Make an Impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical and product direction for a core area of Customer Agent, from architecture through production, and contribute to the direction of the platform overall.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on the hardest technical problems in your area: orchestration, evaluation, guardrails, memory &amp;amp; context, failure handling for non-deterministic systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and ship code, review designs, and make the hard calls in your area when there’s no obvious right answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define patterns that other engineers adopt, and mentor through design reviews rather than direct management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, design, data science, and go-to-market leaders to shape what gets built, not just how it’s built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate emerging AI technologies and bring the ones worth betting on into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built, scaled, and supported production agentic systems, not just prototyped them: real orchestration, evals, guardrails, and non-deterministic failure handling. You&#39;ve owned your part of one through launch, incidents, and the operational reality after the demo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve learned the hard lessons that only come from running agents in production: securing them against misuse and abuse, and the operational scar tissue of keeping a non-deterministic system reliable as usage grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve owned technical and product direction for a significant area before, not just your own component, and you can point to something you designed and championed that shipped and that other engineers built on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re hands-on: writing code, reviewing your own and others’ architecture decisions, and debugging production issues yourself, not delegating the hardest problems away.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your patterns and designs are reused by other engineers, and you&#39;ve unblocked many others’ projects, not just your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate complex technical trade-offs clearly across engineering and product audiences, and you can turn an undefined problem into a plan others rally behind.&lt;/li&gt;
